<title>FRANCE: Details of Jan French crude imports, Feb margins.</title>
<headline>Details of Jan French crude imports, Feb margins.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's industry ministry issued the following data for deliveries to refineries, refining margins and capacity utilisation.</p>
<p>Crude deliveries are by origin ('000 tonnes).</p>
<p>					 Jan 1997   Dec 1996   Jan 1996</p>
<p>    Total				 7,624	7,056	6,958</p>
<p>    Middle East			 2,274	2,507	2,921</p>
<p>    including Saudi Arabia	  1,660	1,823	1,480</p>
<p>		  Iraq			271	    0	    0</p>
<p>		  Iran			258	  523	  965</p>
<p>		  Kuwait		     10	    0	    0</p>
<p>    Africa				1,136	1,302	1,109</p>
<p>    including Algeria		   444	  154	  114</p>
<p>		  Libya			 0	  160	  160</p>
<p>		  Nigeria		   397	  775	  239</p>
<p>    OECD Europe			 3,154	2,837	2,920</p>
<p>    including Britain		 1,281	1,068	1,021</p>
<p>		  Norway		  1,731	1,549	1,666</p>
<p>		  France		    138	  164	  232</p>
<p>    Other				 1,064	  410	    8</p>
<p>    including Venezuela		   0	    0	    0</p>
<p>		  Mexico			0	    0	    0</p>
<p>		  ex-USSR		 1,064	  410	    8</p>
<p>The ministry also released the following data for French refining margins, based on North Sea Brent crude ($/barrel).</p>
<p>			    Feb 1997  Jan 1997  Dec 1996  Jan 1996</p>
<p>    Refining Margin     1.59	2.15	2.19	1.78</p>
<p>In the most recent month for which refinery capacity utilisation is available, French plants ran at 96 percent of capacity in January, up from 89 percent in the strike-hit month of December but down from 97 percent in January 1996.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
</text>
